This license covers the prose, diagrams, and interactive pages of the "Learning
Tock from the Ground Up" series: this file, README.md, and each chapter's
index.html -- which is exactly the set learning/.lcignore excludes from Tock's
own license check.

Two kinds of file under learning/ are not covered, and both carry Tock's
Apache-2.0 OR MIT header instead:

  - the tooling in learning/tools/ and the two ignore files, which are
    repository infrastructure rather than teaching material
  - source a chapter ships so that a figure can be reproduced, such as
    ch01-everything-is-memory/optimizer-demo.rs. That is code, and Creative
    Commons recommend against CC licenses for software, so it takes the license
    of the kernel it demonstrates and can simply be reused.

You are free to:

  Share  -- copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format
  Adapt  -- remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose,
            including commercially

Under the following terms:

  Attribution -- You must give appropriate credit, provide a link to the
                 license, and indicate if changes were made.
  ShareAlike  -- If you remix, transform, or build upon the material, you must
                 distribute your contributions under the same license as the
                 original.

